s8-6-p21 = prose (cons "The first branch precedes every byte access. In the remaining branches \(n\ge4\), so \(n-4\) is defined without unsigned underflow, and the four header reads are in bounds. If \(\ell>n-4\), no output write has occurred. Otherwise \(4+\ell\le n\), so the returned payload view lies within the input allocation; the three output writes touch only the distinct, live \(\mathsf{Frame}\). Header arithmetic is exact since \(0\le b_i<256\) and \(\mathsf{tag},\ell<2^{16}\). The source proof is a term about the *actual interpreted C++ declaration*, not an independently rewritten decoder model. A source annotation can attach the proof through the erasure construction in §6, and its erasure returns this C++ body. Replacing two byte reads by a 16-bit load is a separate transformation whose proof must establish alignment, aliasing, endian interpretation, and memory-validity premises. This example supplies the source-level memory proof distinct from the pure bytecode example in §9." nil)
